\begin{equation}
\theta_{4}(x)=\frac{2\pi}{3}\,
\frac{1+\tanh\!\bigl(\mu x\bigr)}{2},
\end{equation}
linking adjacent $Z_{3}$ vacuum sectors.
Photon propagation couples to $\theta_{4}$ through the effective
index shift
\begin{equation}
\Delta n(x)=\eta\sin^{2}\theta_{4}(x).
\end{equation}
The accumulated phase for wavelength $\lambda$ is
\(
\Delta\phi=(2\pi/\lambda)\int \Delta n(x)\,dx.
\)

